  "Question": "Ryan got \\(80\\%\\) of the problems correct on a \\(25\\)-problem test, \\(90\\%\\) on a \\(40\\)-problem test, and \\(70\\%\\) on a \\(10\\)-problem test. What percent of all the problems did Ryan answer correctly?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 63 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 75 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 80 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 84 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 86 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Every problem contributes equally to the overall percentage, so first count the correct answers on each test. Those counts are\n\\[\n0.80\\cdot25=20,\\qquad\n0.90\\cdot40=36,\\qquad\n0.70\\cdot10=7.\n\\]\nRyan therefore answered \\(20+36+7=63\\) problems correctly out of \\(25+40+10=75\\) problems. His overall percentage is\n\\[\n\\frac{63}{75}=0.84=84\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{84\\%}\\), choice D.",
